    {"type": "arc", "cx": 27, "cy": 24, "r": 11, "a0": 200, "a1": 340, "spacing": 0.7}
  ],
  "start": false,
  "notes": "Plan: Ben's side-view fish, head right at x38-40, forked tail on the left at start (14,20.5), body x16-38, y13-27. I'm building the top edge as an arc (centre 27,24, r 11, angles 200 to 340, spacing 0.7, about 38 dominoes), running from the tail junction (16.7,20.2) over the back (27,13) to the nose (38,20). Ben takes the bottom edge. Ava is on the tail around (14,18.5) and will bridge start into my arc's first domino. Still to do: check the first dominoes turn right, since the start faces up, and check the tail-to-arc join. The scratch pad is with Ben and goes at 2:00. Dev may take the bottom edge after Ben's sketch."
}

{
